    "text": "One rapper's catalog gets played on Spotify seven hundred times a second, and by the time the day closes out, that comes to fifty-nine million plays. Curren$y was on the 2009 XXL Freshman cover, and every song he has ever put on the platform — the mixtapes, the Jet Life run, the features, all of it stacked end to end — adds up to what this one catalog moves in twenty-four days.\n\nAb-Soul falls twenty-eight places, Latto falls thirteen, and Jay Rock falls twelve.\n\nMacklemore keeps seventy-three percent of his streams and drops three spots. Drake loses four point four billion streams, keeps ninety-seven percent of his total, and finishes exactly where he started.\n\nA feature or a remix verse counts at half. That's the 2010 class under the rule, with Nicki at thirty billion and Cole at twenty-nine billion. Now stack all seven careers end to end."
  },
